<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Sacred · date unknown · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="sg-title">Bhaja Govindam</h1><p class="sg-local"><bdi lang="sa">भज गोविन्दम्</bdi> / <bdi lang="sa-Latn">Bhaja Govindam</bdi></p><p class="sg-kid" data-say>A Sanskrit hymn said to be by the teacher Adi Shankara, telling people to praise God instead of wasting their lives on things that pass.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Adi Shankara (traditional attribution; fourteen further verses attributed to his disciples)</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>Hindu devotees: Smarthas, Vaishnavas and others</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Varanasi, India (in the traditional story)</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>traditionally attributed to Adi Shankara; date not known</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Sacred</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (traditionally attributed to Adi Shankara; a medieval Sanskrit hymn)</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>&quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaja-govindam">Bhaja Govindam</a>&quot; (&quot;praise Govinda&quot;, or &quot;seek Govinda&quot;), also called &quot;Moha Mudgara&quot; (&quot;destroyer of illusion&quot;), is a popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> devotional poem in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> traditionally attributed to Adi Shankara. Its opening stanza is a refrain repeated after each verse, as Swami Chinmayananda describes it. The twelve verses after it, the Dvadasa-manjarika-stotram, are traditionally Shankara's own; fourteen more, the Caturdasa-manjarika-stotram, are attributed to fourteen of his disciples. Editions differ in the number, order, wording and arrangement of the stanzas, but not in their meaning. The poem is written in a moraic metre, measured in syllabic instants (mātrās) rather than a fixed number of syllables: apart from the first verse, every verse has sixteen mātrās, the padakulakam of the metrical handbook Vrtta-ratnakara.</p><p>A traditional story tells how it came to be. Walking with his disciples along a street in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanasi">Varanasi</a>, Shankara met an old scholar reciting the rules of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panini">Panini</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> grammar over and over. Taking pity on him, he advised the man not to spend his last years on grammar but to turn his mind to God in worship, which alone could free him from the cycle of birth and death; the hymn is said to have been composed then. It shows that Shankara, often regarded as the reviver of the path of knowledge (jnana marga) to liberation, also taught the path of devotion (bhakti marga), the emphasis of the bhakti movement. In his commentary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/c-rajagopalachari">C. Rajagopalachari</a> wrote that knowledge which has matured is spoken of as devotion, and that knowledge which does not become devotion is &quot;useless tinsel&quot;. Many scholars hold that the poem sums up, briefly and simply, the substance of Shankara's Vedantic thought, and because its refrain invokes God as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> it is sung not only by Shankara's own followers, the Smarthas, but also by Vaishnavas and others.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A call to turn from worldly learning and the ego towards devotion to God and surrender to him, which alone frees a person from the cycle of birth and death; urgent in tone, brought back again and again by its refrain.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-blocks"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-1"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">Sanskrit</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">भजगोविन्दं भजगोविन्दं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">गोविन्दं भजमूढमते ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">संप्राप्ते सन्निहिते काले</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नहि नहि रक्षति डुकृञ्करणे ॥ १॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">मूढ जहीहि धनागमतृष्णां</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कुरु सद्बुद्धिं मनसि वितृष्णाम्।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">यल्लभसे निजकर्मोपात्तं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">वित्तं तेन विनोदय चित्तम् ॥ २॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नारीस्तनभर नाभीदेशं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">दृष्ट्वा मागामोहावेशम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">एतन्मांसावसादि विकारं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">मनसि विचिन्तय वारं वारम् ॥ ३॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नलिनीदलगत जलमतितरलं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">तद्वज्जीवितमतिशयचपलम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">विद्धि व्याध्यभिमानग्रस्तं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">लोकं शोकहतं च समस्तम् ॥ ४॥</span></p></div><details class="sg-more"><summary>Show all 136 lines</summary><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">यावद्वित्तोपार्जन सक्तः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">स्तावन्निज परिवारो रक्तः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">पश्चाज्जीवति जर्जर देहे</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">वार्तां कोऽपि न पृच्छति गेहे ॥ ५॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">यावत्पवनो निवसति देहे</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">तावत्पृच्छति कुशलं गेहे ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">गतवति वायौ देहापाये</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">भार्या बिभ्यति तस्मिन्काये ॥ ६॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">बालस्तावत्क्रीडासक्तः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">तरुणस्तावत्तरुणीसक्तः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">वृद्धस्तावच्चिन्तासक्तः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">परे ब्रह्मणि कोऽपि न सक्तः ॥ ७॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">काते कान्ता कस्ते पुत्रः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">संसारोऽयमतीव विचित्रः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कस्य त्वं कः कुत आयातः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">तत्त्वं चिन्तय तदिह भ्रातः ॥ ८॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सत्सङ्गत्वे निस्स्ङ्गत्वं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">निस्सङ्गत्वे निर्मोहत्वम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">निर्मोहत्वे निश्चलतत्त्वं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">निश्चलतत्त्वे जीवन्मुक्तिः ॥ ९॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">वयसिगते कः कामविकारः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">शुष्के नीरे कः कासारः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">क्षीणेवित्ते कः परिवारः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">ज्ञाते तत्त्वे कः संसारः ॥ १०॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">मा कुरु धन जन यौवन गर्वं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">हरति निमेषात्कालः सर्वम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">मायामयमिदमखिलं हित्वा</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">ब्रह्मपदं त्वं प्रविश विदित्वा ॥ ११॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">दिनयामिन्यौ सायं प्रातः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">शिशिरवसन्तौ पुनरायातः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कालः क्रीडति गच्छत्यायुः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">तदपि न मुञ्चत्याशावायुः ॥ १२॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">द्वादशमञ्जरिकाभिरशेषः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कथितो वैयाकरणस्यैषः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">उपदेशो भूद्विद्यानिपुणैः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">श्रीमच्छन्करभगवच्छरणैः ॥ १२अ ॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">काते कान्ता धन गतचिन्ता</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">वातुल किं तव नास्ति नियन्ता ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">त्रिजगति सज्जनसं गतिरैका</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">भवति भवार्णवतरणे नौका ॥ १३॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">जटिलो मुण्डी लुञ्छितकेशः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">काषायाम्बरबहुकृतवेषः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">पश्यन्नपि चन पश्यति मूढः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">उदरनिमित्तं बहुकृतवेषः ॥ १४॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">अङ्गं गलितं पलितं मुण्डं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">दशनविहीनं जतं तुण्डम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">वृद्धो याति गृहीत्वा दण्डं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">तदपि न मुञ्चत्याशापिण्डम् ॥ १५॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">अग्रे वह्निः पृष्ठेभानुः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">रात्रौ चुबुकसमर्पितजानुः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">करतलभिक्षस्तरुतलवासः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">तदपि न मुञ्चत्याशापाशः ॥ १६॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कुरुते गङ्गासागरगमनं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">व्रतपरिपालनमथवा दानम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">ज्ञानविहिनः सर्वमतेन</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">मुक्तिं न भजति जन्मशतेन ॥ १७॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सुर मंदिर तरु मूल निवासः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">शय्या भूतल मजिनं वासः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सर्व परिग्रह भोग त्यागः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कस्य सुखं न करोति विरागः ॥ १८॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">योगरतो वाभोगरतोवा</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सङ्गरतो वा सङ्गवीहिनः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">यस्य ब्रह्मणि रमते चित्तं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नन्दति नन्दति नन्दत्येव ॥ १९॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">भगवद् गीता किञ्चिदधीता</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">गङ्गा जललव कणिकापीता ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सकृदपि येन मुरारि समर्चा</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">क्रियते तस्य यमेन न चर्चा ॥ २०॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">पुनरपि जननं पुनरपि मरणं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">पुनरपि जननी जठरे शयनम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">इह संसारे बहुदुस्तारे</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कृपयाऽपारे पाहि मुरारे ॥ २१॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">रथ्या चर्पट विरचित कन्थः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">पुण्यापुण्य विवर्जित पन्थः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">योगी योगनियोजित चित्तो</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">रमते बालोन्मत्तवदेव ॥ २२॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कस्त्वं कोऽहं कुत आयातः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">का मे जननी को मे तातः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">इति परिभावय सर्वमसारम्</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">विश्वं त्यक्त्वा स्वप्न विचारम् ॥ २३॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">त्वयि मयि चान्यत्रैको विष्णुः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">व्यर्थं कुप्यसि मय्यसहिष्णुः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">भव समचित्तः सर्वत्र त्वं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">वाञ्छस्यचिराद्यदि विष्णुत्वम् ॥ २४॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">शत्रौ मित्रे पुत्रे बन्धौ</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">मा कुरु यत्नं विग्रहसन्धौ ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सर्वस्मिन्नपि पश्यात्मानं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सर्वत्रोत्सृज भेदाज्ञानम् ॥ २५॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कामं क्रोधं लोभं मोहं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">त्यक्त्वाऽत्मानं भावय कोऽहम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">आत्मज्ञान विहीना मूढाः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">ते पच्यन्ते नरकनिगूढाः ॥ २६॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">गेयं गीता नाम सहस्रं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">ध्येयं श्रीपति रूपमजस्रम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नेयं सज्जन सङ्गे चित्तं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">देयं दीनजनाय च वित्तम् ॥ २७॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सुखतः क्रियते रामाभोगः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">पश्चाद्धन्त शरीरे रोगः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">यद्यपि लोके मरणं शरणं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">तदपि न मुञ्चति पापाचरणम् ॥ २८॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">अर्थमनर्थं भावय नित्यं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नास्तिततः सुखलेशः सत्यम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">पुत्रादपि धन भाजां भीतिः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सर्वत्रैषा विहिआ रीतिः ॥ २९॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">प्राणायामं प्रत्याहारं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नित्यानित्य विवेकविचारम् ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">जाप्यसमेत समाधिविधानं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">कुर्ववधानं महदवधानम् ॥ ३०॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">गुरुचरणाम्बुज निर्भर भकतः</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">संसारादचिराद्भव मुक्तः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">सेन्द्रियमानस नियमादेवं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">द्रक्ष्यसि निज हृदयस्थं देवम् ॥ ३१॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">मूढः कश्चन वैयाकरणो</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">डुकृञ्करणाध्ययन धुरिणः ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">श्रीमच्छम्कर भगवच्छिष्यै</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">बोधित आसिच्छोधितकरणः ॥ ३२॥</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">भजगोविन्दं भजगोविन्दं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">गोविन्दं भजमूढमते ।</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नामस्मरणादन्यमुपायं</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="sa">नहि पश्यामो भवतरणे ॥ ३३॥</span></p></div></details></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Original: traditional text (Sanskrit Wikisource). Text from <a href="https://sa.wikisource.org/wiki/%E0%A4%AD%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%97%E0%A5%8B%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%A6%E0%A4%AE%E0%A5%8D" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; public domain.</p></div></section>
